You are helping plan the next episodes of @talkingagents, an Instagram Reels series (3D animated, 40-60 s, vertical).
Characters: Cleo, a developer (human), and Claude, her AI assistant (a calm, dry-witted glowing character on her screen).
Each episode is a short two-person dialogue, ~14-18 lines, no narrator, no text hook in the first frame, opening line usually starts "Claude, ...".

Two formats the owner LIKES:
1. CLASSIC comedy: a relatable developer disaster, escalating reveals, Claude's deadpan one-liners, a twist punchline at the end.
   Example (Ep10 "Test email sent to 40,000 customers"): Cleo's test email went to the real customer list; replies escalate (manager thumbs-up, CEO "What is this?"); punchline: the test email's 61% open rate beat marketing's 12%.
2. BOARD: Cleo hits a confusing tech problem, Claude says "Board time." and explains it on a whiteboard with one simple metaphor, Cleo applies the fix, it works, a small joke at the end.
   Example (Ep15 "CORS: works in Postman, blocked in Chrome"): different port = different origin; Chrome checks the API's "guest list"; fix is Access-Control-Allow-Origin on the server; "Guests don't write the guest list."

Formats to AVOID for now: nature-documentary / narrated / descriptive style, and emotional no-lesson stories.

Already done (don't repeat): imposter syndrome; API key pushed to GitHub ($2,000 bill); AI refactor broke working code; useEffect infinite loop (45,000 DB reads); CSS fixes sent to the wrong localhost; side project trumpet button; save button solved by her own old Stack Overflow answer; password reset was a 2019 TODO; sharing a localhost link; test email to 40,000 customers; merge conflict force push; two hours to center a div; fetch() doesn't reject on a 500; CORS; git bisect; power cut / battery 3%.
Best views so far: useEffect loop (3.0k), trumpet side project (3.0k), AI refactor broke code (2.9k), password reset TODO (2.1k), API key leak (2.1k). Weakest: center a div (1.4k), imposter syndrome remake (1.5k).

Task: propose 8 new episode ideas: 4 CLASSIC and 4 BOARD. Each must be a very searchable, very relatable topic (things developers actually google or have lived through), with a concrete visual for the 3D scene.
For each idea give:
- Title (short)
- Format (CLASSIC or BOARD)
- Searchable keyword people google (e.g. "why is my API key exposed")
- Opening line (Cleo's first line, starts "Claude, ...", no setup text)
- The beats in 3-5 short bullets (for BOARD: the metaphor and the fix; for CLASSIC: the escalation and the twist)
- Final line / punchline
- Why it should get views (one line)
Then rank your top 3 overall with one line each. Plain text, no tables. Keep it tight.

